      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Echocardiography has gained increasing importance as an imaging modality in the care of the cardiac transplant recipient. Its utility in detecting the complications of transplantation, with special reference to the diagnosis of rejection and graft arteriosclerosis, is discussed. On the basis of a review of the current literature, an outline for serial echocardiographic studies is proposed."},
